menu "telltale — device health metrics"

    config TELLTALE_MAX_WATCHED_TASKS
        int "Maximum tasks whose stack headroom is reported"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
            Each watched task costs one metric slot and a few bytes of RAM.
            The reported value is the FreeRTOS high-water mark, the smallest
            free stack that task has ever had, which is the number that
            predicts an overflow.

    config TELLTALE_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Stack size of the telltale collector task, in bytes"
        default 3072
        range 2048 8192
        help
            The collector samples the heap, the clock and the radio and then
            sleeps. 3 kB is comfortable; raise it if you push OTLP from the
            same task on a target with TLS enabled.

    config TELLTALE_ENABLE_WIFI_COLLECTOR
        bool "Collect Wi-Fi link metrics (RSSI, channel, association)"
        default y
        help
            Requires the esp_wifi component. Disable on Ethernet-only or
            radio-less builds to drop the dependency and three metric slots.

    config TELLTALE_ENABLE_HTTP_ENDPOINT
        bool "Serve GET /metrics over HTTP"
        default y
        help
            Exposes the Prometheus text exposition format on a port of your
            choosing. The endpoint has no authentication: it is meant for a
            trusted network segment or behind a reverse proxy.

    config TELLTALE_ENABLE_OTLP
        bool "Push metrics to an OTLP/HTTP endpoint"
        default y
        help
            Sends the registry as an OTLP/HTTP JSON export request. Use this
            when devices cannot be scraped — behind NAT, on a cellular link,
            or asleep most of the time.

endmenu
